{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1464010286,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNTYyODEzMjM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/457","origin":"github"},"title":"Standardize handling of .git for submodules.","message":"Currently, `.git` of a submodule can end up in various shapes and forms depending on the particular procedure used. It can be:\n1. a .git file\n2. a symlink to ...../.git/modules/...\n3. an actual .git directory\n\nA symlink sometimes leads to a problem: http://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/git-annex_confuses_Git_with_nested_submodules\n\nbut in general all three scenarios seems to work. However, we should discuss which option we are standardizing on (if anyhow possible). Current `install()` implements platform assumptions for `.git` handling that are invalid and ignore direct mode peculiarities.\n\nA solution to this issue would help identify the proper fix.","files":null}]}